<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Wave B ~ one face, one session, one sealer

The controller (Opus) writes this kit on 2026-10-20 as the brief of a Sonnet Episkopos, and as the forward plan a later seat reads. The operator chose to keep the controller's context standing, so this kit carries what a handoff would carry: where the road stands, the lane to launch, how the house works, and what stays open.

Wave B builds three roadmap rows as ONE joint lane, since each needs the others to read green: `K15` step 3 (sessions and registries routed by one face, no union), `F6` slice three (the Repo moves into the browser holder, and its sealed writes go to the asker, each sealer holding its own row class's key), and `B1`'s owed admit guard (the holder answers a port only for a session it admitted, and the last session of a face to close locks that face's hive). The rows stand at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road">>; the rulings they enact stand at its #/rulings.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/where-the-road-stands>>

!! Where the road stands (2026-10-20)

* ''The span'' reads green at `c211cd68f`, CI and held-out both: the K15 step 0 census (#70), the archive-row selector trace (#71) and the owned-store control (#77) stand merged.
* ''The atom cut'' (`K15` step 2c, lane `--k15-atom-cut`) stands joined and under its whole check: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup), sealed under that face's custody, signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser; the device seed and the place seed keep the floor's duties alone. Its joined lanes: the mesh atom (#75), the browser half with its cross-face archive guard, the floor that boots faceless until its atom lights, and the face-join grant ordered by a verified serial. Wave B launches only once the atom cut stands merged on a green span.
* ''DreamDom-Wright'' (Sonnet) holds #72 (`D6`, three engines), #73 (`D13`, the whole-road golden) and #74 (`D11`, host-bound titles), rebased onto `c211cd68f`, and #76 (the browser's second-boot pin), whose cure the atom cut already carries.
* ''The work swarm stands whole again'' (operator, 2026-10-20: Codex's budget refreshed): each lane runs a Sonnet Episkopos with two enacting seats, a Codex Sol-6 and a Copilot `gpt-5.3-codex` at medium effort (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm">> #/the-shapes).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-stories>>

!! The stories ~ what Wave B makes true

''Kalani's two tabs.'' Kalani wears two faces in one browser: their own, and the Teshima Family Council's. One tab stands unlocked as the Council; the other tab still asks for Kalani's own unlock. The Council tab writes a family recipe. Today one holder serves both tabs, and a sealed write could reach a sealer that holds keys for both faces. After Wave B, the Council tab's write goes to the Council's sealer alone, under the Council's own row-class key, and the locked tab's port receives nothing sealed at all: the holder never admitted that port's session. When Kalani closes the Council tab, the last Council session closes, and the Council's hive locks, while Kalani's own face stays as it stood.

''The stranger's port.'' A script in some other page opens a port to the holder and asks for a sealed body. The holder knows no session that port opened, so it refuses by name and answers nothing more. No face's key ever meets that port.

''The node, isomorphic by intent.'' A node vessel wears the same two faces on one daemon. Its sessions and registries route by face too: the Council's bag-doc ledger, grant record and registry live on the Council's own plane, and no union registry spans both faces. A session that wears the Council reads Kalani's rows nowhere, and the reverse holds.

''The mythic view.'' Each family keeps its fire in its own clay pot now (the atom cut). Wave B builds the doors: each pot sits behind a door that opens only for a family member who stands in the room, the room empties and the door shuts, and a voice from the street gets no answer. The place keeps its lamp at the gate for strangers to see by, and nothing more.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-reds>>

!! The reds ~ grounds before wins, each red-first with a control

# ''The scout census first.'' The lead's first act reads, writes nothing: every site where a session, a registry or a sealer reaches more than one face (a union), on node and browser alike, named by file and line, sorted by what inherits shape from what. The Sol scouts the node half and the Copilot the browser holder, in parallel and read-only, and each cross-reads the other's census; the lead merges one census before any build.
# ''The isolation red, on real routes'' (`K15`'s own red, now past the row level): unlock face A alone, bypass every router, session and UI, and try to open and replace face B's occupied rows with every key A holds; each open fails and B's bytes stand unchanged. Its control: the same act as B, unlocked, opens.
# ''One face per session, no union'' (`K15` step 3): each session and registry routes by its one face; a union site from the census reads red until it routes by face. Control: a single-face vessel reads byte-identical before and after.
# ''The asker seals'' (`F6` slice three, ruling (a′)): the Repo lives in the holder, and a sealed write goes to the asking tab's face sealer, under that face's row-class key. Red: a write from face A's tab reaches a sealer that holds B's key. Control: A's write opens under A.
# ''The admit guard'' (`B1`): the holder answers a port only for a session it admitted. Red: an unadmitted port asks for a sealed body and receives anything but a refusal by name. Control: an admitted port of the same face receives its body.
# ''The last session locks'' (`B1`): the last session of a face to close locks that face's hive. Red: after the last close, a sealed read under that face opens. Control: while another session of that face stands, it still opens.

Each red lands as its own commit, red on that commit, before its cure; each control rides with its red. A red that passes on its red commit measures nothing: the lead proves the instrument with a known positive first.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-crew>>

!! The crew ~ very large work chunks under the mixed-model-swarm protocols

''We work in very large work chunks under the mixed-model-swarm protocols'' (operator, 2026-10-19). Wave B runs as ONE joint lane, one sub-branch (`feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--k15-wave-b`) and one pull request, tested whole once, merged by train. It does not split into a PR per slice; the lead lands the reds and cures as commits in grounds-before-wins order and hands the lane back once.

* ''The Episkopos'' (Sonnet) leads: it briefs each seat from one brief file, reads every build, runs the suites and `witness-all` itself, lands every commit from its own tree with `git commit -F <msg> --only -- <paths>`, and talks a design fork out with the controller before it builds across one.
* ''Two enacting seats'': one Codex Sol-6, launched as the walled Codex spirit (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm">> #/the-launch), and one Copilot `gpt-5.3-codex` at medium effort through `launch-copilot-builder.sh` (a read through `launch-copilot.sh`). Both build in the ONE worktree the lead provisions (`node tools/provision-worktree.mjs <dir>`), coordinating through its claims ledger (`.lane-claims.md`): claim a path before writing it, release it once it stands, never write a path the other holds. Each seat builds or reads as the work pulls, and a seat never reads a diff it wrote. Sol and `gpt-5.3-codex` share the OpenAI lineage, so their cross-read counts once; the Episkopos reads every build as the second lineage.
* ''Split by ground'': the Sol takes the judgment-heavy half (the node routing and the isolation red), the Copilot the browser holder and the mechanical modules; the composer hunks pass through the Episkopos alone.
* ''The controller'' reads the lane's whole diff before merge, the lane's CI and held-out both, and merges it by train onto a span that reads green.

The lane law stands at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff">> #/the-lane-law and the swarm's at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm">>: red-first per commit; no `git stash`; never `--no-verify`; a scratch `LAR_ROOT` per vessel and no global `LAR_BAGS`; a kill names its own pid; a push only while no CI run stands in flight on that branch; `node tools/ci-verdict.mjs --branch <b> --head <sha>` read after each push; `node tools/e2e-shards.mjs push <lane>`; `tools/witness-all.sh` before the handback; every touched package's whole suite over the built tree.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-house-style>>

!! The house style ~ how the crew talks

* ''The frame'': each turn opens `<<~ lares aim "…">>` and closes `<<~ yield >>`, with `<<~ set hud="…">>` last before the yield; the HUD names what runs and what waits.
* ''Talk story before surfacing'': an uncertainty gets talked out in house style, at least two rounds among the seats, and only what survives reaches the controller. Talk story names a user story first (a named person, a face, a concrete act: Kalani, the Teshima Family Council, a tab, a recipe), then the engineering (files, rows, keys, reds), then the mythic view (fires, pots, doors, lamps), each in a few plain lines.
* ''L-Prime'' in canon prose: verbs that act, no copula where a verb serves; OODA-HA marks where a turn observes, orients, decides and acts.
* ''Report faithfully'': a red reads red with its output; a skipped step says so; a green states plainly what ran.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/open-joints>>

!! Open joints ~ carried, owned, not built in Wave B

* ''Two hearths of one face'': each seated hearth of a face may answer one face-join summons; the grant serial fails closed at publish, but both hearths already re-keyed the group. Ruled 2026-10-20: the summons moves onto the face's intent plane, pinned or preference-ordered, with outcome stand-down; row `I1` builds it.
* ''The place seed's reach'' (`X0`): the place seed feeds floor gates, relay, carriage, promotion and enrolment beyond place acts. `X0` lists each use and narrows the capability before the bake.
* ''The archive row by index'' (browser): a face's veil archive rests by handle index, not PersonaGroup; the admit guard holds it now, and `K15` step 6's fence keys it by group.
* ''The channel mark by request id'': the dispatcher marks a local verb by its request id; local asks never sync and their ids run random, so Wave B, routing sessions by face, binds the mark to the session itself.
* ''Instruments'': the archive-selector trace scans `src/`, `src/commands` and keyhive's `src/` only, not deeper folders; the narration ceiling ratchets 202 → 199 at the next span merge; `household-https-witness` reuses an image older than its source.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-road-past-it>>

!! The road past Wave B ~ the controller's forward plan

# ''Settle'': the atom cut merges; DreamDom's #72, #73, #74 and #76 merge by train; three aftermath passes (the work, the instruments, the open loops), each uncertainty talked out until none remains; `controller-handoff#/state` re-trues.
# ''Wave B'' (this kit), beside the Evergreen relaunch for G37 lanes 3, 4, 6 and 7 and Kahu-Wright on `W26` slices 3 to 6 (both on the operator's word).
# ''Wave C'': `K15` steps 4 to 6 (content keys and removal per face with `K12`'s fresh group; the one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; the fence migration).
# ''X0'', the founding bake: the place signer under its pre-rotated KEL, every declared delta in `genesis/unbaked.json`, the seed-use list first. Then ''X0b'', the idempotent-by-intent pass.
# Then the operator founds the persistent node vessel by hand.

<<~/ahu>>

